# ---- Fly onboarding retries (hub only, optional) ----
# The fly-onboard-drain block in bin/fly-pool-tick.sh (*/2) runs
# bin/fly-onboard.sh for every project queued in fly/onboard-queue.conf. Each
# attempt spends an image build and a real probe machine, so it is bounded:
#   FLY_ONBOARD_MAX_ATTEMPTS  attempts before it gives up and writes ONE
#                             [fly-onboard] line to logs/ALERTS.log. Default 3.
#   FLY_ONBOARD_RETRY_MIN     minutes between attempts. Default 360 (6h).
# Ledger: state/fly-onboard/<project>.attempts and .last. To re-arm after a
# give-up, remove those and flags/alerted-fly-onboard-gaveup-<project>.
#FLY_ONBOARD_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
#FLY_ONBOARD_RETRY_MIN=360

